          "text": "Now the code-behind for SettingsWindow. Careful about names and event hookups.\n\n```csharp\nusing System.Diagnostics;\nusing System.Windows;\nusing System.Windows.Controls;\nusing System.Windows.Media;\nusing System.Windows.Threading;\nusing WinForms = System.Windows.Forms;\n\nnamespace TaskbarMonitor;\n\npublic partial class SettingsWindow : Window\n{\n    private readonly MeterView _preview = new();\n    private readonly DispatcherTimer _statusTimer;\n    private readonly List<Action> _colorRefreshers = new();\n    private readonly List<UIElement> _colorEditors = new();\n    private BlockSettings? _selectedBlock;\n    private bool _loading;\n\n    private sealed record MonitorEntry(string Device, string Display);\n\n    public SettingsWindow()\n    {\n        InitializeComponent();\n        PreviewHost.Content = _preview;\n        BuildChoices();\n        BuildColorRows();\n        LoadFromSettings();\n        HookEvents();\n        UpdatePreview(true);\n        UpdateStatus();\n\n        _statusTimer = new DispatcherTimer { Interval = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2) };\n        _statusTimer.Tick += (_, _) => UpdateStatus();\n        _statusTimer.Start();\n        Closed += (_, _) => _statusTimer.Stop();\n    }\n```\n\n`BuildChoices`: ThemeCombo.ItemsSource = new[]{\"Auto\",\"Light\",\"Dark\"}; FontCombo...; NetUnitCombo...\nColors rows.\n\n`BuildColorRows`:\n```csharp\nAddColorRow(\"Panel background\", () => s.BackgroundColor, v => s.BackgroundColor = v); ...\n```\nBut callbacks need App.Settings; at construction App.Settings exists. Use lambdas referencing App.Settings directly.\n\nRow creation:\n```csharp\nprivate void AddColorRow(string title, Func<string> get, Action<string> set)\n{\n    var row = new Grid { Margin = new Thickness(0, 3, 0, 3), Tag = (get, set) };\n    row.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = new GridLength(160) });\n    row.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = GridLength.Auto });\n    row.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = GridLength.Auto });\n    var label = new TextBlock { Text = title, VerticalAlignment = VerticalAlignment.Center };\n    var button = new Button { Width = 46, Height = 22, Padding = new Thickness(0), Margin = new Thickness(0), BorderBrush = ..., BorderThickness = new Thickness(1) };\n    var hex = new TextBlock { VerticalAlignment = VerticalAlignment.Center, Margin = new Thickness(10,0,0,0), FontFamily = new FontFamily(\"Consolas\"), FontSize = 12, Foreground = ...};\n    button.Click += (_, _) => PickColor(get(), set);\n    Grid.SetColumn(button, 1); Grid.SetColumn(hex, 2);\n    row.Children.Add(label); row.Children.Add(button); row.Children.Add(hex);\n    ColorsPanel.Children.Add(row);\n    _colorEditors.Add(row);\n    _colorRefreshers.Add(() => { var c = Palette.Parse(get(), Colors.Gray); button.Background = new SolidColorBrush(c); hex.Text = get(); });\n}\n```\n`Tag` unused; drop.\n\nPickColor:\n```csharp\nusing var dialog = new WinForms.ColorDialog { FullOpen = true, AnyColor = true };\nvar current = Palette.Parse(hex, Colors.Gray);\ndialog.Color = System.Drawing.Color.FromArgb(current.R, current.G, current.B);\nif (dialog.ShowDialog() == WinForms.DialogResult.OK)\n{\n    set(Palette.ToHex(Color.FromRgb(dialog.Color.R, dialog.Color.G, dialog.Color.B)));\n    RefreshColors();\n    Apply();\n}\n```\nNote: WinForms ColorDialog.ShowDialog() without owner — fine (uses active window). Could pass no owner.\n\n`RefreshColors()` calls each refresher, enables/disables based on ShowOnAll? No, based on UsePaletteCheck.\n\n`UpdateColorAvailability`: foreach editor IsEnabled = !UseThemePalette.\n\n`LoadFromSettings`:\n```csharp\n_loading = true;\nvar s = App.Settings;\nThemeCombo.SelectedItem = s.Theme;\nUsePaletteCheck.IsChecked = s.UseThemePalette;\nSizeSlider.Value = s.FontSize; SizeValue.Text = $\"{s.FontSize:0}\";\nSpacingSlider.Value = s.Spacing; ...\nOpacitySlider.Value = s.BackgroundOpacity; ...\nFontCombo.SelectedItem = s.FontFamily;\nNetUnitCombo.SelectedItem = s.NetUnit;\nAllMonitorsCheck.IsChecked = s.ShowOnAllMonitors;\nGapSlider.Value = s.GapFromTray;\nRightOffsetSlider.Value = s.OffsetFromRight;\nVerticalSlider.Value = s.OffsetY;\nStartWithWindowsCheck.IsChecked = s.StartWithWindows;\nStartElevatedCheck.IsChecked = s.StartElevated;\nPopulateMonitors(s);\nRefreshColors();\nUpdateColorAvailability();\nRebuildBlocks();\nif (_selectedBlock != null) SelectBlock(_selectedBlock) else ShowDetails(null);\n_loading = false;\n```\n\nCareful: `_selectedBlock` may reference a stale object after Reset. Set to null in Reset before Load. Or find block by Kind:\n```csharp\nvar selectedKind = _selectedBlock?.Kind;\n_selectedBlock = selectedKind is null ? null : s.Blocks.FirstOrDefault(b => b.Kind == selectedKind);\n```\nDo this at the start of LoadFromSettings.\n\n`PopulateMonitors`:\n```csharp\nvar screens = WinForms.Screen.AllScreens;\nvar entries = screens.Select(sc => new MonitorEntry(sc.DeviceName, $\"{sc.DeviceName} — {sc.Bounds.Width}×{sc.Bounds.Height}{(sc.Primary ? \"  (primary)\" : \"\")}\")).ToList();\nMonitorCombo.ItemsSource = entries;\nvar selected = entries.FirstOrDefault(e => string.Equals(e.Device, s.MonitorDevice, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n               ?? entries.FirstOrDefault(e => screens.Any(sc => sc.Primary && sc.DeviceName == e.Device))\n               ?? entries.FirstOrDefault();\nMonitorCombo.SelectedItem = selected;\nMonitorCombo.IsEnabled = !s.ShowOnAllMonitors;\n```\nActually matching primary: entries built in same order; simpler: `entries.FirstOrDefault(e => e.Device == s.MonitorDevice) ?? entries.FirstOrDefault()`. Settings.MonitorDevice empty → first (Display1 primary). But AllScreens order might not have primary first. Find primary index: \n```csharp\nvar primary = screens.FirstOrDefault(sc => sc.Primary);\nMonitorCombo.SelectedItem = entries.FirstOrDefault(e => e.Device == s.MonitorDevice)\n                            ?? entries.FirstOrDefault(e => e.Device == primary?.DeviceName)\n                            ?? entries.FirstOrDefault();\n```\nWhen user changes selection → settings.MonitorDevice = ((MonitorEntry)MonitorCombo.SelectedItem).Device.\n\n`HookEvents`:\n```csharp\nThemeCombo.SelectionChanged += (_,_) => Apply();\nUsePaletteCheck.Checked += (_,_) => { UpdateColorAvailability(); Apply(); };\nUsePaletteCheck.Unchecked += ...\nFontCombo.SelectionChanged += ...\nSizeSlider.ValueChanged += (_,_) => { SizeValue.Text = $\"{SizeSlider.Value:0}\"; Apply(); };\n...\nAllMonitorsCheck.Checked/Unchecked += (_,_) => { MonitorCombo.IsEnabled = AllMonitorsCheck.IsChecked != true; Apply(rebuildOverlays: true); };\nMonitorCombo.SelectionChanged += (_,_) => Apply(rebuildOverlays: true);\nStartWithWindowsCheck... -> ApplyStartup()\nStartElevatedCheck...\n```\nSince Apply() reads controls.\n\n`ReadControls`:\n```csharp\nvar s = App.Settings;\ns.Theme = ThemeCombo.SelectedItem as string ?? \"Auto\";\ns.UseThemePalette = UsePaletteCheck.IsChecked == true;\ns.BackgroundOpacity = Math.Round(OpacitySlider.Value, 2);\ns.FontFamily = FontCombo.SelectedItem as string ?? \"Segoe UI\";\ns.FontSize = Math.Round(SizeSlider.Value);\ns.Spacing = Math.Round(SpacingSlider.Value);\ns.NetUnit = NetUnitCombo.SelectedItem as string ?? \"Mbps\";\ns.ShowOnAllMonitors = AllMonitorsCheck.IsChecked == true;\nif (MonitorCombo.SelectedItem is MonitorEntry entry) s.MonitorDevice = entry.Device;\ns.GapFromTray = Math.Round(GapSlider.Value);\ns.OffsetFromRight = Math.Round(RightOffsetSlider.Value);\ns.OffsetY = Math.Round(VerticalSlider.Value);\n```\nStartup handled separately, but also read here for persistence:\n```csharp\ns.StartWithWindows = StartWithWindowsCheck.IsChecked == true;\ns.StartElevated = StartElevatedCheck.IsChecked == true;\n```\n\n`Apply(bool rebuildOverlays=false)`:\n```csharp\nif (_loading) return;\nReadControls();\nApp.ApplySettings();\nif (rebuildOverlays) App.RebuildOverlays();\nRefreshColors();  // colors may have changed only by picker; keep\n```\nBut RefreshColors recreates brushes each Apply; cheap. However if called while the user hasn't changed colors, fine.\n\nPotential recursion: `Apply` → `App.ApplySettings` → `SettingsWindowInstance.UpdatePreview` → fine.\n\n`UpdatePreview(bool rebuild)`:\n```csharp\nif (rebuild) _preview.Apply(App.Settings, App.CurrentPalette);\nelse _preview.ApplyStyle(App.Settings, App.CurrentPalette);\n_preview.UpdateValues(App.Latest);\n```\n\nBlocks UI:\n\n```csharp\nprivate void RebuildBlocks()\n{\n    BlocksPanel.Children.Clear();\n    foreach (var block in App.Settings.Blocks.OrderBy(b => b.Row).ThenBy(b => b.Order))\n    {\n        var grid = new Grid { Height = 36 };\n        grid.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = new GridLength(34) });\n        grid.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = new GridLength(1, GridUnitType.Star) });\n        grid.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = GridLength.Auto });\n        grid.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = new GridLength(34) });\n        grid.ColumnDefinitions.Add(new ColumnDefinition { Width = new GridLength(34) });\n\n        var check = new CheckBox { IsChecked = block.Enabled, VerticalAlignment = VerticalAlignment.Center, Margin = new Thickness(10,0,0,0) };\n        check.Click += (_, _) => { block.Enabled = check.IsChecked == true; Apply(); RebuildBlocks(); };\n```\nClicking triggers rebuild immediately, which recreates the checkbox while the mouse is over it — acceptable but might cause a flicker; also the click event completes. Use `check.Checked/Unchecked` to set and Apply without rebuilding (no ordering change). Just Apply, no RebuildBlocks (the visual stays). Fine.\n\nText: `block.Kind.Title()`; label with muted style? Use normal.\n\nRow combo:\n```csharp\nvar rowCombo = new ComboBox { Width = 80, SelectedIndex = block.Row - 1, VerticalAlignment = VerticalAlignment.Center };\nrowCombo.ItemsSource = new[] { \"Row 1\", \"Row 2\" };\nrowCombo.SelectionChanged += (_, _) => { if (_loading) return; var newRow = rowCombo.SelectedIndex + 1; if (newRow == block.Row) return; block.Row = newRow; block.Order = App.Settings.Blocks.Count(b => b.Row == newRow); Apply(); RebuildBlocks(); };\n```\nHmm block.Order may collide with the max order; Normalize will fix ordering but add duplicates? `Normalize` re-numbers sequentially sorted by Order; colliding order values sort stably (List order). Fine.\n\nButtons:\n```csharp\nvar up = SmallButton(\"▲\", () => MoveBlock(block, -1));\nvar down = SmallButton(\"▼\", ...);\n```\nUse \"↑\"/\"↓\" text, width 28, padding 0, margin 2.\n\nAssemble with Grid.SetColumn.\n\nBorder card background: selected ? `#EAF3FB` : White; border color.\n\nClick on border: `MouseLeftButtonUp` → SelectBlock(block).\n\nNote: clicking on a Button inside also bubbles to Border? MouseLeftButtonUp handled by Button then bubbles up to Border too, causing selection — harmless.\n\n`SelectBlock(block)`:\n```csharp\n_selectedBlock = block;\nDetailsEmpty.Visibility = Collapsed;\nDetailsBody.Visibility = Visible;\nDetailsTitle.Text = block.Kind.Title();\n_loading = true; // avoid Apply on checkbox assignments\nLabelBox.Text = block.Label ?? \"\";\nChkIcon.IsChecked = block.ShowIcon;\nChkLabel.IsChecked = block.ShowLabel;\nChkPercent.IsChecked = block.ShowPercent && block.Kind.SupportsPercent();\nChkTemp.IsChecked = block.ShowTemperature && block.Kind.SupportsTemperature();\nChkPower.IsChecked = block.ShowPower && block.Kind.SupportsPower();\n_loading = false;\nChkPercent.IsEnabled = block.Kind.SupportsPercent();\nChkTemp.IsEnabled = block.Kind.SupportsTemperature();\nChkPower.IsEnabled = block.Kind.SupportsPower();\nChkTemp.Visibility = Supports ? Visible : Collapsed; // better than disabled\n...\nRebuildBlocks(); // for highlight\n```\nCareful: RebuildBlocks called from SelectBlock which is called from LoadFromSettings → fine. But SelectBlock → RebuildBlocks → each row click handlers. No recursion into SelectBlock.\n\nAlso RebuildBlocks called from SelectBlock, which rebuilds and might lose selection? _selectedBlock remains; highlight uses reference equality → works.\n\nDetails events (hooked once in HookEvents):\n```csharp\nLabelBox.TextChanged += (_,_) => { if (_loading || _selectedBlock is null) return; _selectedBlock.Label = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(LabelBox.Text) ? null : LabelBox.Text.Trim(); Apply(); };\n```\nBut Apply rebuilds the preview; does it rebuild blocks? No. Label change doesn't need RebuildBlocks. However overlay updates. Good.\n\nCheckbox handlers:\n```csharp\nvoid Detail(CheckBox box, Func<BlockSettings, bool> get, Action<BlockSettings, bool> set)\n```\nSimpler individual lambdas with `_selectedBlock`.\n\n`ChkIcon.Checked/Unchecked` → bool value = ChkIcon.IsChecked == true.\n\nAfter changing ShowIcon, view needs rebuild → Apply() calls App.ApplySettings(rebuild: true) which rebuilds. Good.\n\nStartup:\n```csharp\nprivate void StartupChanged()\n{\n    if (_loading) return;\n    App.Settings.StartWithWindows = StartWithWindowsCheck.IsChecked == true;\n    App.Settings.StartElevated = StartElevatedCheck.IsChecked == true;\n\n    if (App.Settings.StartWithWindows && App.Settings.StartElevated && !App.IsElevated)\n    {\n        var answer = MessageBox.Show(this, \"Elevated startup needs administrator rights once...\\n\\nRestart as administrator now?\", \"Taskbar Monitor\", MessageBoxButton.YesNo, MessageBoxImage.Question);\n        if (answer == MessageBoxResult.Yes) { App.RestartElevated(); return; }\n        _loading = true;\n        StartElevatedCheck.IsChecked = false;\n        _loading = false;\n        App.Settings.StartElevated = false;\n    }\n\n    Startup.Apply(App.Settings.StartWithWindows, App.Settings.StartElevated);\n    UpdateStatus();\n    App.QueueSave();\n}\n```\n\nRestartAdmin_Click: confirm and restart.\n\nOpenFolder_Click: `Process.Start(new ProcessStartInfo { FileName = SettingsStore.Folder, UseShellExecute = true })`.\n\nUpdateStatus:\n```csharp\nElevationBadge.Text = App.IsElevated ? \"Administrator\" : \"Standard user\";\nCpuStatusText.Text = App.Metrics.CpuTemps.InitializationFinished\n   ? \"CPU temperature: \" + App.Metrics.CpuTemps.Status\n   : \"CPU temperature: reading sensors…\";\nGpuStatusText.Text = App.Metrics.Gpu.Available\n   ? \"GPU sensors: NVML ready.\"\n   : \"GPU sensors: no NVIDIA GPU detected (GPU values show --).\";\nStartupStatusText.Text = App.Settings.StartWithWindows\n   ? (App.Settings.StartElevated ? \"Startup: scheduled task with highest privileges.\" : \"Startup: current-user Run key.\")\n   : \"Startup: disabled.\";\n```\n`App.Metrics.Gpu.Available` may become true after async init? NVML init is synchronous in Start. Fine.\n\nFooterStatus maybe show transient messages, leave as is.\n\n`ResetDefaults_Click`:\n```csharp\nif (MessageBox.Show(this, \"Reset every setting to its default?\", \"Taskbar Monitor\", MessageBoxButton.YesNo, MessageBoxImage.Question) != MessageBoxResult.Yes) return;\nApp.ResetSettings();\n_selectedBlock = null;\n_loading = true;\nLoadFromSettings();  // but LoadFromSettings sets _loading itself; nested guard fine\n_loading = false;\nRebuildBlocks();\nUpdatePreview(true);\nUpdateStatus();\n```\n`LoadFromSettings` sets `_loading = true` then false — outer setting is overwritten. Fine.\n\nApp.ResetSettings implementation not yet added → add.\n\n`Close_Click` → Close().\n\nAlso handle window closed → App.SettingsWindowInstance = null already via App subscription.\n\nOne more: `UpdatePreview` called by App tick: if the window is closing? `SettingsWindowInstance` null after Closed. Fine.\n\n`MonitorCombo.SelectionChanged` during LoadFromSettings: _loading guard in Apply, but the handler also sets nothing besides Apply. Good.\n\nNote `PopulateMonitors` sets `SelectedItem` which fires SelectionChanged → Apply guarded by _loading (true during LoadFromSettings). Good.\n\nWrite the code-behind now, plus App.ResetSettings and remove dead `ApplyStyle